  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-hh-left-left-yetter-drinfeld-module": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $H$ be a Hopf algebra over a field $k$. A **left-left Yetter–Drinfeld $H$-module** is a $k$-vector space $V$ with a bilinear left action $H\\otimes V\\to V$, $(h,v)\\mapsto h\\cdot v$, satisfying $1_H\\cdot v=v$ and $(hh')\\cdot v=h\\cdot(h'\\cdot v)$, and a left coaction $\\delta:V\\to H\\otimes V$, $\\delta(v)=\\sum v_{-1}\\otimes v_0$, satisfying\n\n$$\\sum (\\Delta\\otimes\\operatorname{id})\\delta(v)=\\sum (\\operatorname{id}\\otimes\\delta)\\delta(v),\\qquad (\\varepsilon\\otimes\\operatorname{id})\\delta(v)=v,$$\n\nand the compatibility equation\n\n$$\\delta(h\\cdot v)=\\sum h_1v_{-1}S(h_3)\\otimes h_2\\cdot v_0.$$\n\nA morphism is a $k$-linear map preserving both action and coaction. For $f\\in H^*$ define $f\\cdot v:=\\sum f(v_{-1})v_0$. With convolution $(f*g)(x)=\\sum f(x_1)g(x_2)$ and opposite product $f\\odot g=g*f$, this is a left $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}$-action."
    ],
    "def-hh-finite-double-cross-relations": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $k$ be a field and let $H$ be a finite-dimensional Hopf algebra over $k$ with bijective antipode $S$. Write $H^*=\\operatorname{Hom}_k(H,k)$. Its dual coproduct is the unique map $\\Delta_{H^*}:H^*\\to H^*\\otimes H^*$ satisfying\n\n$$\\Delta_{H^*}(f)(x\\otimes y)=f(xy)$$\n\nfor all $f\\in H^*$ and $x,y\\in H$; finite tensor duality ensures this is an algebraic tensor. The ordinary convolution product on $H^*$ is $(f*g)(x)=\\sum f(x_1)g(x_2)$. We use the **opposite algebra** $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}$, whose product is $f\\odot g:=g*f$ and whose coproduct is the ordinary dual coproduct, not its opposite.\n\nAs a vector space set $D(H):=H^{*\\mathrm{op}}\\otimes H$ and write $fh$ for $f\\otimes h$ in this normal order. Define the crossing map\n\n$$\\chi(h\\otimes f)=\\sum f_1(S(h_1))f_3(h_3)f_2\\otimes h_2.$$\n\nThe candidate product and unit are\n\n$$ (f\\otimes h)(g\\otimes k)=\\sum g_1(S(h_1))g_3(h_3)(g_2*f)\\otimes h_2k,\\qquad 1_D=\\varepsilon_H\\otimes 1_H. $$\n\nThe appearance of $g_2*f$ is the $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}$ product $f\\odot g_2$. This item defines the bilinear candidate operation; associativity, the coalgebra structure and the antipode are supplied separately by [[lem-hh-double-crossing-map-and-associativity]] and [[lem-hh-double-coalgebra-and-antipode-descent]]."
    ],
    "lem-hh-double-crossing-map-and-associativity": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the candidate crossing $\\chi$ and product on $D(H)$ in [[def-hh-finite-double-cross-relations]], $\\chi$ is unital and satisfies both distributive laws for multiplication in $H$ and $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}$. Consequently the candidate product is associative and unital, with injective algebra embeddings $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}\\hookrightarrow D(H)$ and $H\\hookrightarrow D(H)$ in normal order."
    ],
    "lem-hh-double-coalgebra-and-antipode-descent": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the associative algebra $D(H)$ of [[lem-hh-double-crossing-map-and-associativity]], define\n\n$$\\Delta_D(fh)=\\sum (f_1h_1)\\otimes(f_2h_2),\\qquad \\varepsilon_D(fh)=f(1_H)\\varepsilon_H(h).$$\n\nThese maps make $D(H)$ a bialgebra. The inverse crossing, in normal order, is\n\n$$fh=\\sum f_1(h_1)f_3(S(h_3))h_2f_2.$$\n\nMoreover,\n\n$$S_D(fh):=S(h)(f\\circ S^{-1})$$\n\nis an antipode. Thus $D(H)$ is a Hopf algebra with the stated normal-order formulas."
    ],
    "thm-hh-double-modules-and-yetter-drinfeld-modules": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $H$ be a finite-dimensional Hopf algebra over a field with bijective antipode, and let $D(H)$ be the finite double above. Restriction to $H$ and reconstruction of a coaction from the $H^{*\\mathrm{op}}$ action give inverse equivalences between left $D(H)$-modules and left-left Yetter–Drinfeld $H$-modules. The equivalence preserves tensor products. The Yetter–Drinfeld category is braided by\n\n$$c_{V,W}(v\\otimes w)=\\sum v_{-1}\\cdot w\\otimes v_0,$$\n\nwith inverse\n\n$$c_{V,W}^{-1}(w\\otimes v)=\\sum v_0\\otimes S^{-1}(v_{-1})\\cdot w.$$"
    ],
    "thm-hh-finite-double-hopf-structure-and-canonical-r": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $H$ be a finite-dimensional Hopf algebra over a field with bijective antipode, and let $(h_i)$ and $(f_i)$ be dual bases of $H$ and $H^*$. In the factor order $D(H)=H^{*\\mathrm{op}}\\otimes H$, the tensor\n\n$$R=\\sum_i(f_i\\otimes1_H)\\otimes(\\varepsilon_H\\otimes h_i)$$\n\nis basis-independent and invertible, with\n\n$$R^{-1}=\\sum_i(f_i\\otimes1_H)\\otimes(\\varepsilon_H\\otimes S^{-1}(h_i)).$$\n\nIt is quasitriangular in the convention\n\n$$R\\Delta_D(d)=\\Delta_D^{\\mathrm{op}}(d)R,\\qquad(\\Delta_D\\otimes\\operatorname{id})R=R_{13}R_{23},\\qquad\\alpha^{-1}_{D,D,D}(\\operatorname{id}\\otimes\\Delta_D)R=R_{13}R_{12}.$$\n\nOn every pair of left $D(H)$-modules, $\\tau\\circ R$ is the Yetter–Drinfeld braiding of [[thm-hh-double-modules-and-yetter-drinfeld-modules]]."
    ],
